title: The Moscow Compromise
subtitle: The International proposes places for the Left in the Zentrale.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 5 and left_formed = 1 and left_expelled = 0 and leader = "right"
max-visits: 1

= The Moscow Compromise

Since Leipzig the Left has run Berlin and Hamburg almost as a second party. In April the International called both camps to Moscow. Its proposal: the Zentralausschuss co-opts four leaders of the Left into the Zentrale, Ruth Fischer, Ernst Thälmann, Ottomar Geschke and Arthur König, and the Left accepts the Zentrale's discipline.

- @accept
- @refuse

@accept
title: Co-opt the four into the Zentrale.
subtitle: Calms the <span class="f-left">Left</span> and pleases Moscow. Some of the <span class="f-right">Right</span> resent it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_in_zentrale = 1;
Q.left_dissent -= 15;
Q.right_dissent += 4;
Q.left_moscow += 4;
Q.right_moscow += 3;
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

On 17 May the Zentralausschuss elects the four. For the first time in months the Zentrale speaks for the whole party, at least on paper.

@refuse
title: Keep the Zentrale in the majority's hands.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span>. The <span class="f-left">Left</span> is furious, and Moscow is displeased.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_in_zentrale = 0;
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 3});
Q.left_dissent += 15;
Q.right_moscow -= 8;
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

The majority says the congress has spoken. In Berlin the district leadership prints its own leaflets.
